      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T10:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t mean a property literally called \"src\" or \"srcs\" but rather some property that serves that function. The generic Prebuilt struct looks like this:\n\ntype Prebuilt struct {\n\tproperties PrebuiltProperties\n\n\tsrcsSupplier     PrebuiltSrcsSupplier\n\tsrcsPropertyName string\n}\n\nWhen I use src/srcs I am referring to those fields in Prebuilt.\n\nI am not 100% sure what happens if you don\u0027t have a source module and the prebuilt does not have a valid srcs property. It may be that the prebuilt is used anyway in that case. However, if you have both source and prebuilt then the source will be used even when the prebuilt is preferred which would be incorrect.",
